<header class="site-header">
  <div class="container">
    <a class="site-title" href="{{ site.base_url | escape }}/">
      <img src="/images/rust-9000-48.png" width="24" height="24" alt="">
      {{ site.title | escape }}
    </a>
  </div>
</header>

{% comment %}
  No scroll-into-view and no drawer: both need JavaScript, and the order is the stack order the rail
  exists to teach. The current hub comes from the permalink, which every page has -- `page.data.hub`
  is set only on hub pages, and reading a missing key off an empty `data` is an error, not nil.
{% endcomment %}
{% assign here = page.permalink | remove: "/" %}
<nav class="rail" aria-label="Topic hubs">
  <div class="container rail-inner">
    {% for hub in site.data.topics %}
    <a class="rail-chip rail-chip-{{ hub.color | escape }}{% if here == hub.id %} rail-chip-current{% endif %}"
       href="/{{ hub.id | escape }}"{% if here == hub.id %} aria-current="page"{% endif %}>{{ hub.short | escape }}</a>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
</nav>
